9. Boot  hub

From power button to login prompt: firmware, bootloader, kernel, init.

On your machine
  Firmware  UEFI · Secure Boot on
  Kernel    6.12.48-amd64
  Cmdline   BOOT_IMAGE=/vmlinuz-6.12.48-amd64
            root=UUID=3f1c2a9e-8b7d-4e21-9c55-0a6b2d7e9f10 ro rootflags=subvol=@
            quiet splash
  Init      systemd · default target graphical.target
  Up        3 days, 4 h

Commands
  systemd-analyze        how long the last boot took, by stage
  systemd-analyze blame  services, slowest first
  journalctl -b -p err   errors logged since this boot
  systemctl get-default  the target the system boots into
  efibootmgr             UEFI boot entries and their order
  uname -r               the running kernel

Paths
  /proc/cmdline      options the kernel was started with
  /boot              kernels and initramfs images
  /etc/default/grub  GRUB settings, kernel options included

Cards
  idk 9.1  From firmware to init
  idk 9.2  The kernel command line
